            "telephone": "+84 90 149 64 49",
            "review_id": "REV_16670988_p1_0",
            "reviewer_id": "User_16670988_1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at The Colour Craft Beer",
            "review_text": "Moving_Goujon\n84 contributions\n0\nAn absolute p***take\nMar 2020 • Couples\nIn passing we were lured in by the promises of craft beer, and being sonewhat peckish we thought we might grab a bite to eat. Two beers ordered and a plate of nachos, all is well.\n\nUntil the nachos arrived... Or pretty much didn't!\n\n135,000 for maybe ten nachos and a dollop of brown slop. Now we have put up with and tolerated some pitiful offerings of sustenance in Vietnam but this was an absolute insult. I brought our disappointment to the attention of a waiter and he went to get 'the manager', who told us that seeing as we are 'new to his establishment' he would provide us with a little extra. Trust me when i say that a double helping would have been a rip off, so i argued that i no longer wanted to eat here. We were told in no uncertain terms that this was not an option and we would still have to pay for the order, so reluctantly we agreed.\n\nFive extra nachos and more brown slop arrived. No joke, five nachos! In disbelief we ate and asked for the bill, upon receiving it we had been charged more than the menu stated for the drinks we had purchased. Having remembered how much they were listed as in the menu i again protested, and the bill was eventually reduced accordingly with a nonsensical justification for the 'mistake' and apology from the poor sods that have to work here.\n\nThis establishment, or rather those running it, do not deserve your custom!! You can get nice beer and better food from any number of other establishments in HCM city that wont treat you like an idiot in the process. Avoid at all costs, this place is the pits!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 13, 2020",
